{100}{}{Phil}
{200}{}{You see a peasant.}
{210}{}{You see Phil.}
{1000}{}{I wouldn't trust that beast, if I was you. That thing is a killer.}
{1001}{}{Thanks for your help.}
{1002}{}{Damn right, shoot that beast!}
{1003}{}{Mister,
---
Ma'am,
---
I would be really happy if you were to get rid of that damn dog.}
{1004}{}{I hate that dog.}
{1005}{}{It won't let us back into our house, that's why.}
{1006}{}{It was the 'pet' of a traveller. When the traveller died, this damn dog just plopped its
furry ass down on my doorstep and wouldn't leave. It's been there for days.}
{1007}{}{Mebbe you can talk it to death.}
{1008}{}{So, Gizmo had a couple of boys beat him up and throw him from the casino roof. The
traveller broke his damnfool neck and died. The dog was pissed.
---
I don't know. Some guy. He came from the east, he said. Like anyone could get past the
deadlands to the east. He ran afoul of Gizmo, trying to interfere with Gizmo's business.}
{1009}{}{He had some funny accent. The dog was his constant companion, followed him everywhere.
---
Oh, the guy was tall, dark-haired with a little graying around the edges. He was dressed
all in black leather, like that's a good idea in the desert, and carried a shotgun.}
